==Cat Capsules+==
An addition added in the [[Version 11.0 Update]] and released in the [[Version 11.1 Update]]. The upgrade to the regular Cat Capsule can be obtained after beating [[Cats of the Cosmos#Chapter 3: Even Stars Burn Out|Even Stars Burn Out]] of [[Cats of the Cosmos]]. The Normal Cat Capsule will be upgraded to a Cat Capsule+ which makes all the cat units obtained from it sell for 2 NP rather than 1 and adds a new basic cat ([[Superfeline (Normal Cat)|Superfeline]]) to the pool as well as increasing the 64 storage limit to 128, similar to the [[Catfruit]] storage prior to the [[Version 11.4 Update|Version 11.4]] update.

==Rare Capsule==
===Regular Gacha===
[[File:Raregacha en.png|thumb|200x200px|Rare Capsule Banner]]
[[File:GatyaitemD 21 f.png|thumb|100x100px|A Rare Cat Ticket]]
[[File:Rare cat capsule.png|thumb|200x200px]]
From time to time, the player can get a '''Rare Cat Ticket''', by purchasing it with [[Cat Food]], clearing certain stages, trading 5 Ability Capsules or as Stamp Rewards. These tickets can be used at any time to roll the Rare Capsule. After rolling the Rare Capsule, the player will get a '''Gacha Cat''' ([[:Category:Rare Cats|Rare]], [[:Category:Super Rare Cats|Super Rare]], [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Rare]] or [[:Category:Legend Rare Cats|Legend Rare Cats]]). Each new unit will reward 5 Cat Food as when checked in the Cat Guide. Most, if not all, Gacha units are included in at least one [[Cat Combo]].

If the player gets a Gacha Cat they already have, they can use it as an upgrade for the same cat, as long as the unit has not reached their maximum plus level. This is the only way to pass the maximum level cap (using only XP) of Level 30 (alongside using [[Catseye]]s up to level 50/60). Generally, these duplicates should be used, and not traded; the additional levels will be immensely helpful in the long run. Units only useful for [[:Category:Crowd-Controller-class Cats|crowd-control]], such as [[Onmyoji Cat (Rare Cat)|Thaumaturge Cat]], likely won't benefit much from plus levels and thus the NP is probably more useful. As with [[:Category:Normal Cats|Normal Cats]], it's best to wait until any stats-based unit is maxed out before exchanging one for NP, and you should ''never'' trade any unit for XP, as it's far, far easier to get than NP.

Most of the time, the rarity of the Cat fixes their interval of cost (Uber Rare Cats' cost is usually over 3,000¢, for example) and their power (you expect an Uber Rare Cat to be stronger than a Rare Cat). Thus, Uber Rare Cats and Legend Rare Cats are more desirable, but are usually not a direct replacement for more common units.

It is important to understand that the '''Rare Capsule roll-result sequence is predetermined''' by an account-specific seed, this seed then determines the roll-result sequence, which can be gamed to some extent by waiting for various Gacha events to appear before rolling. That helps in obtaining a desired Uber Rare Cat in a shorter time (fewer rolls) by filling the next preset Uber Super Rare roll-result slot with one from the available pool of Gacha Event Uber Rare Cats. The roll-result sequence is actually made up of two sequences / 'tracks', and doing a 11 roll during a [[Guaranteed Uber Rare Cat Campaign]] will switch between the tracks on the last roll.

While the normal cat capsule has a different seed than the rare capsule, the rare capsule shares its seed with the [[Platinum Capsules (Gacha Event)|Platinum Capsule]] and [[Legend Capsules (Gacha Event)|Legend Capsule]].

Gacha events advertising a boosted drop rate i.e. 'increased chance' of obtaining [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber Super Rare]] Cats will displace what would otherwise be a non-Uber Super Rare Cat roll-result at a preset positions in the ladder with an Uber Super Rare Cat from the event. This doesn't affect the subsequent roll-result sequence, until the next displacement and so on.

'''Note: Saving Rare Cat Tickets does NOT provide an option for 11-capsule draws.'''

The Uber Rare Cats and Legend Rare Cats that one can get are fixed on a schedule. Usually, the pool of Uber/Legend Rare Cats changes every two days. Before playing the Rare Capsule, the player can see the actual pool. From time to time, additional Super Rare Cats are added.<gallery hideaddbutton="true">
Rarecapsule.png|The Rare Capsule
</gallery>

===Collaboration Cats===
During some [[:Category:Collaboration Events|Collaboration Events]], the player is given the option to roll another pool, filled with new Cats inspired by the collaboration. This pool may have only [[:Category:Collaboration Event Cats|Collaboration Cats]] or possibly a combination of Collaboration Cats and regular Gacha cats. The Collaboration Gacha was introduced during the [[Monster Hunter Collaboration Event]] in the Japanese Version, and the [[Survive! Mola Mola! Collaboration Event]]s in the English Version.

===Limited Gacha===
This Gacha follows the same rules as a Collaboration Gacha. These pools tend to contain regular Uber Rare Cats with a new appearance, a new ability and sometimes new stats. Examples are the Holiday events, such as [[Gals of Summer Sunshine (Gacha Event)|Gals of Summer Sunshine]] and [[Halloween Capsules (Gacha Event)|Halloween Capsules]], and [[Girls & Monsters: Angels of Terror (Gacha Event)|Girls & Monsters]], which includes characters from [[GirlsMons]] and [[Kyoutou Project]].

===Cost of the Rare Capsule===
''Note: You can only purchase instant draws. Thus, you cannot purchase a discounted 11-capsule draw then save it for another pool... If you already have Rare Cat Tickets, you have to use them before purchasing single draws.''

::'''1 Draw'''
*Normal: 150 Cat Food
*First Time Offer: 30 Cat Food
*Discounted Offer: 120 Cat Food
::'''11 Draws'''
*Normal: 1500 Cat Food
*First Time Offer: 750 Cat Food
*Discounted Offer: 1200 Cat Food

During every Gacha event except [[UBERFEST (Gacha Event)|UBERFEST]], [[EPICFEST (Gacha Event)|EPICFEST]], and [[SUPERFEST (Gacha Event)|SUPERFEST]], a [[Guaranteed Uber Rare Cat Campaign]] may be held, in which a Uber Rare Cat is guaranteed when doing an 11-capsule draw. The guaranteed Uber will always replace the 11th unit.

During the [[RED BUSTERS (Gacha Event)|RED BUSTERS]], [[AIR BUSTERS (Gacha Event)|AIR BUSTERS]], [[METAL BUSTERS (Gacha Event)|METAL BUSTERS]], [[WAVE BUSTERS (Gacha Event)|WAVE BUSTERS]] and [[Colossus Busters (Gacha Event)|Colossus Busters]] events, a [[Increasing Capsules Campaign|Step Up]] option with three steps appears.
* Step 1: 300 Cat Food for 3 draws.
* Step 2: 750 Cat Food for 5 draws, plus a 1 million XP bonus.
* Step 3: 1050 Cat Food for 7 draws, plus a 1 million XP bonus. In addition, the 7th unit is guaranteed to be an Uber Rare Cat.
After purchasing a Step 3 spin, or after 30 minutes have passed after purchasing a Step 1 spin, the current Step will revert to 1.

==Platinum Capsule==
The [[Platinum Capsules (Gacha Event)|Platinum Capsule]] is an uncommon type of Cat Capsule that will appear whenever you have a Platinum ticket or shard. It requires Platinum Tickets to spin, which can be obtained with real money or as special rewards. This capsule will always drop Uber Rare Cats. Only one may be purchased per appearance, though there is no limit to how many a player can hold.

==Collaboration Event Capsule==
Aside from the regular and Rare Capsule, there are limited collaboration capsules that arrive during certain collaborations, most notably [[Monster Hunter Collaboration Event|Monster Hunter]], [[Nebaaru-kun and Nyanpazuru Collaboration Event|Nebaaru-kun and Nyanpazuru]] and [[Bikkuriman Collaboration Event|Bikkuriman]].

These limited collaboration gachas have a chance to drop items from the regular [[Cat Capsule#Lucky Capsules|Lucky Capsule]] as well as units from said collaborations.

*''See [[Monster Hunter Collaboration Event/Event Gacha]], [[Nebaaru-kun and Nyanpazuru Collaboration Event/Event Gacha]] and [[Bikkuriman Collaboration Event/Event Gacha]].''

